{"ts": "2026-11-21T15:37:55.240746Z", "run_id": "r-20261121T1533Z-5a3a", "unit": "openspec:restyle-web-kit-followup-1", "seq": 14, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-001", "target": "C-6027f26f", "decision": "accept", "by": "agent", "reason": "The criterion is satisfied, and the delegate verified it by hand. Ignored test e2e/test_run_header_meta.py::test_page_header_meta_wraps_below_the_title_with_gaps does discriminate. On the offline e2e stack with web built at the unit head 563f4585 it passes at 1366 and 390. With web/src/kit/theme.css put back to main's and web rebuilt, it fails: AssertionError, at 1366px meta item 0 starts at or below the title's bottom edge: 80 vs 116. It asserts the scenario as written: the status and the five items below the h1, the first within 1 px of the h1's left edge, items whose tops are within 4 px at least 8 px apart, the h1 on one line, and assert_layout at both widths. The CSS change (.ui-page-header-meta spanning the grid as a wrapping flex row with a gap; actions at row 1, column 2) is identical to the fix I tried on main 36dd7cce, where all 118 e2e tests and the 17 Node tests that read theme.css passed and the Home, Flow and Policies headers still read well.", "text_sha256": "a851c293400583c13f03d2f2a4d3a8bd96648bdb0b4606f274f831bb683ed189", "answer_sha256": "4fe667192cc7a00b0955e982920cf0fbf3d968e4d2d386dfc8df08be46d2d1f9", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
